.TH AICAMPRO 1 "2026-08-20" "AICamPro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aicampro \- AI webcam with background removal, accelerated on AMD GPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aicampro
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AICamPro
removes, blurs or replaces your webcam background, grades colour, retouches
and auto-frames you, then offers the result to other applications as a virtual
camera. Every per-frame operation runs on the GPU through PyTorch on ROCm.
.PP
The GPU runtime is not part of this package. Run
.BR aicampro-setup (1)
once before the first launch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Report the compute device, the matting models found, and every camera and
virtual camera on the system, then exit. This is the first thing to run when
something does not work.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
List cameras and v4l2loopback devices, marking which of the latter actually
accept a video stream, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " PATH"
Use this camera instead of the one stored in the configuration, for example
.IR /dev/video0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read settings from this file instead of the default.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Toggle the virtual camera output.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Start or stop recording.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save a snapshot.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AICAMPRO_PYTHON
Interpreter to run the application with, overriding the managed environment.
.TP
.B AICAMPRO_MODEL_DIR
Directory holding the matting models. Defaults to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/aicampro/models .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aicampro/config.json
Settings, written on exit.
.TP
.I ~/.config/aicampro/presets/
Saved presets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/aicampro/venv/
The GPU runtime created by
.BR aicampro-setup (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on a clean exit, non-zero if the runtime is missing or the camera
cannot be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aicampro-setup (1),
.BR v4l2loopback-ctl (1)
.PP
Full documentation at
.UR https://github.com/hashcott/AICamPro
.UE
